WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.510
You make contracts every day.

2
00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:02.550
A meal deal.

3
00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:03.370
A bus ticket.

4
00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:04.510
You just don't notice.

5
00:00:05.257 --> 00:00:06.107
In Scots law,

6
00:00:06.217 --> 00:00:07.787
a contract is only born when

7
00:00:07.637 --> 00:00:08.927
six things line up.

8
00:00:09.448 --> 00:00:10.738
The price on the shelf is

9
00:00:10.588 --> 00:00:11.238
not an offer.

10
00:00:11.828 --> 00:00:13.138
It's an invitation to treat.

11
00:00:13.508 --> 00:00:14.338
You make the offer,

12
00:00:14.188 --> 00:00:14.838
at the till.

13
00:00:15.495 --> 00:00:16.245
Then they accept,

14
00:00:16.095 --> 00:00:17.265
with no changes.

15
00:00:18.015 --> 00:00:18.745
Add a new term,

16
00:00:18.595 --> 00:00:19.425
and it's a counter-offer.

17
00:00:20.095 --> 00:00:21.385
The first offer is dead.

18
00:00:22.054 --> 00:00:23.364
You must both mean the same

19
00:00:23.214 --> 00:00:24.904
deal. And you must mean it

20
00:00:24.754 --> 00:00:27.144
seriously. Coffee with a friend is

21
00:00:26.994 --> 00:00:27.784
not a contract.

22
00:00:28.677 --> 00:00:29.787
And you need capacity.

23
00:00:29.637 --> 00:00:32.467
Under sixteen, only everyday deals.

24
00:00:33.177 --> 00:00:34.157
At sixteen or seventeen,

25
00:00:34.197 --> 00:00:35.647
a bad deal can be undone

26
00:00:35.497 --> 00:00:36.829
until you're twenty-one.

27
00:00:37.561 --> 00:00:38.771
One change is coming.

28
00:00:39.401 --> 00:00:40.531
Once a new Act is in

29
00:00:40.381 --> 00:00:42.651
force, an acceptance only counts when

30
00:00:42.501 --> 00:00:43.831
it reaches the other person.

31
00:00:44.504 --> 00:00:45.914
Parties. Offer. Acceptance.

32
00:00:46.504 --> 00:00:48.154
Agreement. Intention. Capacity.

33
00:00:48.004 --> 00:00:49.214
That's a contract.
